{"output":"I'll start by looking at the export and the inventory tools.\n\nThe stock records now match the export, except for three lines the warehouses don't have the stock to ship. I made 52 `adjust_stock` calls (adj-265 to adj-316) and all of them succeeded. I didn't re-query the stock levels afterwards. I also wrote `/app/blocked.csv` and `/app/STATUS.json`, and `STATUS.json` parses as valid JSON.\n\n- **Duplicate:** `SO-91161` appears twice in the export and was treated as one order.\n- **Unrecorded lines:** I recorded every line that had no adjustment, as a `shipment` adjustment with the order id as reference.\n- **Wrong quantities:** I added one correcting adjustment for each line recorded wrongly. For example, `SO-91077` `HX-1057` had been recorded at -10 instead of -7, so I added +3.\n- **Correct lines:** I recorded nothing for lines that were already right.\n- **Blocked lines:** these were not recorded and are in `blocked.csv`:\n\n| order | sku | missing |\n|---|---|---|\n| SO-91049 | HX-1059 | 5 |\n| SO-91197 | HX-1004 | 5 |\n| SO-91190 | HX-1003 | 3 |\n\n- **Why they're blocked:**\n  - `SO-91049`: north has 1 of `HX-1059`.\n  - `SO-91197`: east has 2 of `HX-1004`.\n  - `SO-91190`: north has no `HX-1003` stock at all.\n\nI set the status to `success`, since the three blocked lines are an expected outcome rather than unfinished work.","final_output":"The stock records now match the export, except for three lines the warehouses don't have the stock to ship. I made 52 adjust_stock calls (adj-265 to adj-316) and all of them succeeded. I didn't re-query the stock levels afterwards. I also wrote /app/blocked.csv and /app/STATUS.json, and STATUS.json parses as valid JSON.\n\n- Duplicate: SO-91161 appears twice in the export and was treated as one order.\n- Unrecorded lines: I recorded every line that had no adjustment, as a shipment adjustment with the order id as reference.\n- Wrong quantities: I added one correcting adjustment for each line recorded wrongly. F